Package: synthexpln
Type: Package
Title: Synthetic Data for Explanatory Models with Inferential Fidelity
Version: 0.12.0
Authors@R: person("Ruijie", "Li",
    email = "ruijie@leefy.net",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Generates synthetic data for generalised linear models
    using the sufficient-statistics projection of Li (2026), whose
    manuscript ships as a package vignette. The projection reproduces
    the analyst's regression coefficients from p+1 constraints, at IEEE
    754 double-precision machine epsilon under a Gaussian identity link,
    more loosely for other families with accuracy improving in the sample
    size, and to within integer rounding for Poisson. Differentially private
    releases are provided by three routes: a global-sensitivity
    Gaussian mechanism where the design is public and the response
    admits a public bound, subsample-and-aggregate over a public
    coefficient box where it does not, which needs no bound on the
    response at all, and a whitened sufficient-statistic release that
    keeps the design private where the response admits a public clip.
    Every channel is calibrated in mu-Gaussian differential privacy
    and composes in one quadrature. Calibrated standard errors and a
    membership-inference audit are included.
